Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["WolframGuard", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"f8c4cf52-7dbf-0d49-8626-051deb766345"],

Cell["A containment-based guard for the Wolfram agent evaluator", "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0037320510316296`*^9, 
  4.003732051677334*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"952a8f7b-fb4f-7a41-a7af-\
f05dd5c48e3d"],

Cell["\<\
When an AI agent is handed the Wolfram Language evaluator as a tool, the only \
thing standing between a prompt-injected DELETE and your database is a single \
approval click in the chat client. WolframGuard adds a second line of defense \
inside the server. For a read-only task it places an operating-system \
read-only lock on the authorized data, so a write fails at the OS no matter \
which primitive or language the model's code uses, with a parse-before-run \
classifier in front that acts as a fast pre-filter. The policy is one the \
model cannot widen so the worst a prompt injection can do is force a read, \
every other write it attempts fails at the OS lock.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003732073010828*^9, 4.0037320745195255`*^9}, {
  4.0037323601874123`*^9, 4.0037323764196625`*^9}, {4.0037420933918056`*^9, 
  4.003742105591215*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ab54169a-1cd8-0046-9f42-\
f6cedd109788"],

